[Document(metadata={'id': 'safety manual.pdf_p2_c0', 'source': 'safety manual.pdf', 'page_number': 2, 'start_line_number': 1, 'end_line_number': 13
    }, page_content='2\nTHIS SAFETY GUIDEBOOK BRIEFLY EXPLAINS THE OPERATION  \nOF YOUR VEHICLE AND SOME KEY SAFETY FEATURES. \nPLEASE NOTE THAT THIS MANUAL APPLIES TO ALL MODELS AND \nEXPLAINS ALL EQUIPMENT, INCLUDING OPTIONS. THEREFORE, \nYOU MAY FIND SOME EXPLANATIONS FOR EQUIPMENT NOT \nINSTALLED ON YOUR VEHICLE.\nTHE DRIVER IS RESPONSIBLE FOR SAFE DRIVING. ALWAYS DRIVE \nSAFELY AS SAFETY FUNCTIONS ARE SUPPLEMENTARY ONLY, \nTAKING CARE TO OBSERVE YOUR SURROUNDINGS AT ALL TIMES.\npage 3 \n 01  SEATBELTS\npage 4–5'), Document(metadata={'id': 'safety manual.pdf_p2_c1', 'source': 'safety manual.pdf', 'page_number': 2, 'start_line_number': 1, 'end_line_number': 34
    }, page_content='TAKING CARE TO OBSERVE YOUR SURROUNDINGS AT ALL TIMES.\npage 3 \n 01  SEATBELTS\npage 4–5  \n 02  CHILD SAFETY\npage 6–7  \n 03  SRS AIRBAGS\npage 7 \n 04  ABS (ANTI-LOCK BRAKING SYSTEM)\npage 8 \n 05  BRAKE ASSIST\npage 8 \n 06  VSC (VEHICLE STABILITY CONTROL) SYSTEM\npage 9  \n 07  ELECTRONIC BRAKE FORCE DISTRIBUTION\npage 9 \n 08  EMERGENCY BRAKE SIGNAL\npage 9 \n 09  BRAKE OVERRIDE S\npage 10 \n 10  TRAILER SWAY CONTROL\npage 10 \n 11  BLIND SPOT MONITORING & REAR CROSS TRAFFIC ALERT\npage 10 \n 12  HILL ASSIST'), Document(metadata={'id': 'safety manual.pdf_p2_c2', 'source': 'safety manual.pdf', 'page_number': 2, 'start_line_number': 1, 'end_line_number': 41
    }, page_content='page 10 \n 11  BLIND SPOT MONITORING & REAR CROSS TRAFFIC ALERT\npage 10 \n 12  HILL ASSIST\npage 11 \n 13  SMART ENTRY AND START SYSTEM\npage 11 - 13 \n 14  CAUTION WHEN DRIVING AND STOPPING\n \n  \nCONTENT'), Document(metadata={'id': 'safety manual.pdf_p3_c0', 'source': 'safety manual.pdf', 'page_number': 3, 'start_line_number': 1, 'end_line_number': 10
    }, page_content='3\nHow to wear seatbelts correctly  \nAll passengers in the vehicle should fasten their seatbelts at all times.\nSIT WITH CORRECT POSTURE\n•  Position the seat upright and lean your back against the seatback.\n•  Avoid reclining the seatback. If your seat is reclined during  \nan accident, you may slide under the seatbelt – which could  \nresult in serious or life-threatening injuries.\nCORRECTLY FASTEN YOUR SEATBELTS\n•  Position the shoulder belt so it does not come into contact'), Document(metadata={'id': 'safety manual.pdf_p3_c1', 'source': 'safety manual.pdf', 'page_number': 3, 'start_line_number': 9, 'end_line_number': 18
    }, page_content='CORRECTLY FASTEN YOUR SEATBELTS\n•  Position the shoulder belt so it does not come into contact  \nwith your neck or slide off your shoulder.\n•  Position the lap belt low over the pelvis below the abdomen.\n•  Ensure the buckle of the seatbelt clicks firmly into place.\n•  Read more about seatbelt safety for children under  \n‘2 Child Safety’ in this Safety Guidebook.\nFor instructions on how to adjust the seatbelts,  \nplease refer to the owner’s manual for your vehicle.\n 01  SEATBELTS'), Document(metadata={'id': 'safety manual.pdf_p4_c0', 'source': 'safety manual.pdf', 'page_number': 4, 'start_line_number': 1, 'end_line_number': 9
    }, page_content='4\nDO NOT ALLOW CHILDREN TO PLAY WITH PARTS OF THE VEHICLE THAT OPEN AND CLOSE\n•  Children should not be allowed to play with doors or windows as it may cause injuries or accidents.\nDRIVING WITH CHILDREN\n•  Children should be seated in the rear seats.\n•  An adult passenger must be seated next or close to a child to ensure the child’s safety.\n•  Always follow the manufacturer’s instructions when using a child restraint system.\n 02  CHILD SAFETY\nPLACE CHILDREN IN A CORRECT SITTING POSITION'), Document(metadata={'id': 'safety manual.pdf_p4_c1', 'source': 'safety manual.pdf', 'page_number': 4, 'start_line_number': 8, 'end_line_number': 25
    }, page_content='02  CHILD SAFETY\nPLACE CHILDREN IN A CORRECT SITTING POSITION\n•  Do not allow a child to stand up or kneel on the front passenger \nseat, or sit on the lap of a front passenger. The SRS front passenger \nairbag could inflate with considerable speed and force.\n•  When using a child restraint system, please ensure that the child’s \nhead or any other body parts are not leaning against the door, \nseat, front pillar, rear pillar or roof side rail.\nINSTALLING CHILD RESTRAINT SYSTEM'), Document(metadata={'id': 'safety manual.pdf_p4_c2', 'source': 'safety manual.pdf', 'page_number': 4, 'start_line_number': 15, 'end_line_number': 22
    }, page_content='seat, front pillar, rear pillar or roof side rail.\nINSTALLING CHILD RESTRAINT SYSTEM\n•  Child restraint system should be installed on the rear outside seat  \nfollowing the instructions provided by the manufacturer.\n•  When using a bar dedicated for harnessing an ISOFIX-supporting \nchild seat, check that there are no obstacles in surrounding area \nand that the seatbelt has not been caught.\n•  A forward-facing child restraint system should only be installed'), Document(metadata={'id': 'safety manual.pdf_p4_c3', 'source': 'safety manual.pdf', 'page_number': 4, 'start_line_number': 12, 'end_line_number': 25
    }, page_content='•  A forward-facing child restraint system should only be installed \non the front passenger seat when necessary. Always move the \nseat as far back as possible because the front passenger airbag \ncould inflate with considerable speed and force.'), Document(metadata={'id': 'safety manual.pdf_p5_c0', 'source': 'safety manual.pdf', 'page_number': 5, 'start_line_number': 1, 'end_line_number': 10
    }, page_content='5\nPlease refer to the warning of the same contents displayed on  \nthe sun visor on the passenger seat side.\n•  Never install a rear-facing child restraint system on the front \npassenger seat.\n•  When using a booster seat, always ensure the shoulder belt  \nis positioned across the centre of your child’s shoulder. \nDO NOT ALLOW CHILDREN TO PLAY WITH SEATBELTS\n•  If the harness strap is pulled out to the end, the ALR (Automatic \nLocking Retractor) activates and the seatbelt cannot be loosened.'), Document(metadata={'id': 'safety manual.pdf_p5_c1', 'source': 'safety manual.pdf', 'page_number': 5, 'start_line_number': 10, 'end_line_number': 19
    }, page_content='Locking Retractor) activates and the seatbelt cannot be loosened.\n•  If the seatbelt becomes twisted around a child’s neck, it could \nlead to death by choking. If the buckle cannot be unfastened, \nscissors or other sharp tools should be used to cut the belt.\nEQUIPMENT TO AVOID DANGER CAUSED BY INCORRECT \nOPERATION BY CHILD\n•  Child protective door lock \nThis device prevents a child from opening the rear seat  \ndoor from inside.\n•  Window lock switch'), Document(metadata={'id': 'safety manual.pdf_p5_c2', 'source': 'safety manual.pdf', 'page_number': 5, 'start_line_number': 17, 'end_line_number': 27
    }, page_content='This device prevents a child from opening the rear seat  \ndoor from inside.\n•  Window lock switch \nThis device prevents a child from operating the window. \nNEVER LEAVE A CHILD UNATTENDED IN A VEHICLE\n•  The interior temperature of a vehicle parked under sunlight can \nbecome extremely high, and a child can suffer from heatstroke \nand dehydration, which can be fatal. Also, the child could be \ninvolved in an unexpected accident by playing with the vehicle \ncontrols and equipment.\n 02  CHILD SAFETY'), Document(metadata={'id': 'safety manual.pdf_p6_c0', 'source': 'safety manual.pdf', 'page_number': 6, 'start_line_number': 1, 'end_line_number': 34
    }, page_content='6\nSRS Airbags \nSRS (Supplemental Restraint System) airbags are designed \nto provide further protection for the driver and passengers \nin addition to the primary safety protection provided by \nseatbelts. Types of SRS airbags are as follows:\n 1 SRS driver airbag / front passenger airbag \n2 SRS side airbags\nSPECIFICATIONS MAY VARY FROM THE MODELS AVAILABLE.\nSIT WITH CORRECT POSTURE\n•  Do not sit too close to the steering wheel or dashboard.'), Document(metadata={'id': 'safety manual.pdf_p6_c1', 'source': 'safety manual.pdf', 'page_number': 6, 'start_line_number': 2, 'end_line_number': 19
    }, page_content='SIT WITH CORRECT POSTURE\n•  Do not sit too close to the steering wheel or dashboard.  \nThe driver and the front passenger should not hold items  \non their laps.\n•  Do not allow anyone to lean against the door, centre pillar,  \nrear pillar and roof side rail.\n•  Do not allow anyone to kneel on the passenger seat facing  \nthe side door or put their heads or hands out the window.\nSRS AIRBAGS MAY NOT DEPLOY EVEN IN A COLLISION\n•  Examples of SRS airbags not deploying (test vehicle)'), Document(metadata={'id': 'safety manual.pdf_p6_c2', 'source': 'safety manual.pdf', 'page_number': 6, 'start_line_number': 2, 'end_line_number': 35
    }, page_content='•  Examples of SRS airbags not deploying (test vehicle)  \nSRS driver and front passenger airbags\nCOLLISION FROM AN ANGLE COLLISION WITH A SMALL TREE OR  \nOTHER RELATIVELY MOVABLE OBJECT\nCOLLISIONS WHERE THE FORCE OF  \nTHE COLLISION IS DOWNWARD SUCH  \nAS AN IMPACT WITH THE LOADING  \nPLATFORM OF A TRUCK\nCOLLISIONS WHERE THE IMPACT  \nCOMES FROM AN ANGLE\nCOLLISIONS WHERE THE PASSENGER  \nCOMPARTMENT IS NOT DIRECTLY IMPACTED\n 03  SRS AIRBAGS\n1\n12\n2\nFRONT COLLISION AT LOW SPEED'), Document(metadata={'id': 'safety manual.pdf_p7_c0', 'source': 'safety manual.pdf', 'page_number': 7, 'start_line_number': 1, 'end_line_number': 60
    }, page_content='7\n•  Example of deployment in which SRS airbags may not demonstrate \ntheir primary effectiveness.\nIN ROLLS AND TURN OVERS  \nFor details, please refer to the owner’s manual for your vehicle.\nDO NOT ATTACH OBJECTS AROUND THE SRS AIRBAGS\n•  Do not attach objects on areas such as the dashboard, steering \nwheel pad, lower portion of instrument panel, doors, windshield \nglass, front or rear pillar, roof side rail and assist grip.\nABS'), Document(metadata={'id': 'safety manual.pdf_p7_c1', 'source': 'safety manual.pdf', 'page_number': 7, 'start_line_number': 9, 'end_line_number': 50
    }, page_content='glass, front or rear pillar, roof side rail and assist grip.\nABS \nABS (Anti-locking Braking System) prevents wheels from locking up,  \nallowing driver to maintain control over the vehicle under emergency braking situations. \n•  When sudden braking is necessary, step hard on the brake pedal.\n•  Do not pump or let up on the brake pedal.\n•  You will feel fine vibrations on the brake pedal and hear noises –  \nthis indicates that the ABS is active.\nABS WILL NOT SHORTEN BRAKING DISTANCE'), Document(metadata={'id': 'safety manual.pdf_p7_c2', 'source': 'safety manual.pdf', 'page_number': 7, 'start_line_number': 10, 'end_line_number': 70
    }, page_content='this indicates that the ABS is active.\nABS WILL NOT SHORTEN BRAKING DISTANCE\n•  ABS vehicles may take slightly longer to stop on poor-conditioned \nroads; such as roads that are bumpy, stone-paved or uneven.\nReminder: ABS does not eliminate the danger of accidents. Hence, \nalways be sure to drive safely and maintain a safe distance from the \nvehicle in front of you.\n 03  SRS AIRBAGS \n 04  ABS\nBRAKE\nFORCE\nBRAKE\nFORCE\nWithout VSC\nWithout Brake Assist\nWithout ABS\nWith ABS\nBraking Point'), Document(metadata={'id': 'safety manual.pdf_p7_c3', 'source': 'safety manual.pdf', 'page_number': 7, 'start_line_number': 10, 'end_line_number': 70
    }, page_content='BRAKE\nFORCE\nBRAKE\nFORCE\nWithout VSC\nWithout Brake Assist\nWithout ABS\nWith ABS\nBraking Point\nWith Brake Assist\nWithout VSC\nWith VSC\nBA\nWithout TRC With TRC\nWithout VSC\nFront wheel slipping\nSteering loses control\nWithout VSC\nRear wheel slipping\nOver-steering\nWith VSC\nWith ABS\nWithout ABS\nBRAKE\nFORCE\nBRAKE\nFORCE\nWithout VSC\nWithout Brake Assist\nWithout ABS\nWith ABS\nBraking Point\nWith Brake Assist\nWithout VSC\nWith VSC\nBA\nWithout TRC With TRC\nWithout VSC\nFront wheel slipping\nSteering loses control'), Document(metadata={'id': 'safety manual.pdf_p7_c4', 'source': 'safety manual.pdf', 'page_number': 7, 'start_line_number': 10, 'end_line_number': 70
    }, page_content='With VSC\nBA\nWithout TRC With TRC\nWithout VSC\nFront wheel slipping\nSteering loses control\nWithout VSC\nRear wheel slipping\nOver-steering\nWith VSC\nWith ABS\nWithout ABS'), Document(metadata={'id': 'safety manual.pdf_p8_c0', 'source': 'safety manual.pdf', 'page_number': 8, 'start_line_number': 1, 'end_line_number': 47
    }, page_content='8\nBRAKE ASSIST \nBrake Assist helps in emergency situations when pressure on the  \nbrake pedal is insufficient during sudden or ‘panic’ braking.\nVSC (Vehicle Stability Control) system  \nVSC (Vehicle Stability Control) system helps to prevent wheel slip  \nwhen turning a vehicle or during sudden steering situations.\n•  Brake Assist helps to apply full braking force when it detects that the pressure that is applied  \non the brake pedal is insufficient.'), Document(metadata={'id': 'safety manual.pdf_p8_c1', 'source': 'safety manual.pdf', 'page_number': 8, 'start_line_number': 2, 'end_line_number': 56
    }, page_content='on the brake pedal is insufficient.\n•  The system’s computer analyses whether or not to activate Brake Assist based on how fast  \nand hard the driver is stepping on the brake pedal.\n•  The system detects the vehicle’s instability and controls the slide, allowing the driver to maintain \ncontrol of the vehicle. \n \nThe illustration shows what happens to the car after the driver rapidly turns the steering wheel'), Document(metadata={'id': 'safety manual.pdf_p8_c2', 'source': 'safety manual.pdf', 'page_number': 8, 'start_line_number': 2, 'end_line_number': 66
    }, page_content='The illustration shows what happens to the car after the driver rapidly turns the steering wheel \nin mid-corner. With the aid of VSC, the car maneuvers properly and is able to quickly return \nto its original lane.\nReminder: VSC does not eliminate the danger of accidents. It only assists with vehicle stability.\n 05  BRAKE ASSIST  \n 06  VSC (VEHICLE STABILITY CONTROL) SYSTEM\nBRAKE\nFORCE\nBRAKE\nFORCE\nWithout VSC\nWithout Brake Assist\nWithout ABS\nWith ABS\nBraking Point\nWith Brake Assist\nWithout VSC'), Document(metadata={'id': 'safety manual.pdf_p8_c3', 'source': 'safety manual.pdf', 'page_number': 8, 'start_line_number': 2, 'end_line_number': 66
    }, page_content='Without VSC\nWithout Brake Assist\nWithout ABS\nWith ABS\nBraking Point\nWith Brake Assist\nWithout VSC\nWith VSC\nBA\nWithout TRC With TRC\nWithout VSC\nFront wheel slipping\nSteering loses control\nWithout VSC\nRear wheel slipping\nOver-steering\nWith VSC\nWith ABS\nWithout ABS\nBRAKE\nFORCE\nBRAKE\nFORCE\nWithout VSC\nWithout Brake Assist\nWithout ABS\nWith ABS\nBraking Point\nWith Brake Assist\nWithout VSC\nWith VSC\nBA\nWithout TRC With TRC\nWithout VSC\nFront wheel slipping\nSteering loses control\nWithout VSC'), Document(metadata={'id': 'safety manual.pdf_p8_c4', 'source': 'safety manual.pdf', 'page_number': 8, 'start_line_number': 25, 'end_line_number': 66
    }, page_content='BA\nWithout TRC With TRC\nWithout VSC\nFront wheel slipping\nSteering loses control\nWithout VSC\nRear wheel slipping\nOver-steering\nWith VSC\nWith ABS\nWithout ABS'), Document(metadata={'id': 'safety manual.pdf_p9_c0', 'source': 'safety manual.pdf', 'page_number': 9, 'start_line_number': 1, 'end_line_number': 28
    }, page_content='9\n•  During braking while cornering, this function controls the brake force that acts on the left and \nright wheels in accordance with the vehicle condition at that time. This ensures vehicle stability \nand excellent braking performance.\nEMERGENCY BRAKE SIGNAL\n•  The Emergency Brake Signal automatically flashes the hazard warning lights in the case of      \nemergency braking in order to reduce the risk of being rear ended by a following vehicle.'), Document(metadata={'id': 'safety manual.pdf_p9_c1', 'source': 'safety manual.pdf', 'page_number': 9, 'start_line_number': 7, 'end_line_number': 12
    }, page_content='emergency braking in order to reduce the risk of being rear ended by a following vehicle.\n•  The skid control ECU detects the vehicle condition and braking operation using the speed sensors \nand stop light switch assembly.\n•  If emergency braking is detected based on these various signals, the skid control ECU sends a \nsignal to the combination meter assembly to flash the hazard warning lights.\nBRAKE OVERRIDE SYSTEM'), Document(metadata={'id': 'safety manual.pdf_p9_c2', 'source': 'safety manual.pdf', 'page_number': 9, 'start_line_number': 1, 'end_line_number': 35
    }, page_content='signal to the combination meter assembly to flash the hazard warning lights.\nBRAKE OVERRIDE SYSTEM\n•  When both accelerator and brake pedals are depressed, this system may restrain the engine out -\nput and support brake performance.\n 07  ELECTRONIC BRAKE FORCE DISTRIBUTION  \n 08  EMERGENCY BRAKE SIGNAL\n09  BRAKE OVERRIDE SYSTEM\nWithout Load in Rear\nFront Brake Force\nIdeal Brake Force Distribution\nRear Brake\nForce\nEBD Control\nWith Load in Rear\nFront Brake Force\nIdeal Brake Force Distribution'), Document(metadata={'id': 'safety manual.pdf_p9_c3', 'source': 'safety manual.pdf', 'page_number': 9, 'start_line_number': 19, 'end_line_number': 36
    }, page_content='Rear Brake\nForce\nEBD Control\nWith Load in Rear\nFront Brake Force\nIdeal Brake Force Distribution\nRear Brake\nForce\nEBD Control\nWithout Trailer Sway Control\nWith Trailer Sway Control\nSide Wind\nSide Wind Brake Control + Engine Output Control\nWith Hill-Start Assist Control Without Hill-Start Assist Control\nElectronic Brake Force Distribution (EBD)  \nEBD controls the brake force that acts on the rear wheels in accordance with changes in'), Document(metadata={'id': 'safety manual.pdf_p9_c4', 'source': 'safety manual.pdf', 'page_number': 9, 'start_line_number': 22, 'end_line_number': 37
    }, page_content='EBD controls the brake force that acts on the rear wheels in accordance with changes in \nthe vehicle condition in order to ensure excellent braking performance.'), Document(metadata={'id': 'safety manual.pdf_p10_c0', 'source': 'safety manual.pdf', 'page_number': 10, 'start_line_number': 1, 'end_line_number': 8
    }, page_content='10\n•  Trailer Sway Control reduces the yaw motion by decelerating the vehicle and creating counter  \nmoments to the tow vehicle.\n•  Trailer Sway Control is a part of the VSC function. Accordingly, if the VSC OFF mode is selected or \nVSC is not functioning normally, trailer sway control will not operate.\nBLIND SPOT MONITORING / REAR CROSS TRAFFIC ALERT\n•  The blind spot monitor system performs two functions using the same sensors: Blind Spot Monitor \nand Rear Cross Traffic Alert.'), Document(metadata={'id': 'safety manual.pdf_p10_c1', 'source': 'safety manual.pdf', 'page_number': 10, 'start_line_number': 1, 'end_line_number': 69
    }, page_content='and Rear Cross Traffic Alert.\n•  The blind spot monitor function uses sensors to detect vehicles that are traveling in the vehicle’s \nblind spot, helping the driver to confirm safety when changing lanes.\n•  The Rear Cross Traffic Alert functions detects a vehicle in the rear side direction which the driver is \nreversing.\n 10  TRAILER SWAY CONTROL \n 11  BLIND SPOT MONITORING & REAR CROSS TRAFFIC ALERT \n12  HILL ASSIST\nWithout Load in Rear\nFront Brake Force\nIdeal Brake Force Distribution'), Document(metadata={'id': 'safety manual.pdf_p10_c2', 'source': 'safety manual.pdf', 'page_number': 10, 'start_line_number': 15, 'end_line_number': 75
    }, page_content='12  HILL ASSIST\nWithout Load in Rear\nFront Brake Force\nIdeal Brake Force Distribution\nRear Brake\nForce\nEBD Control\nWith Load in Rear\nFront Brake Force\nIdeal Brake Force Distribution\nRear Brake\nForce\nEBD Control\nWithout Trailer Sway Control\nWith Trailer Sway Control\nSide Wind\nSide Wind Brake Control + Engine Output Control\nWith Hill-Start Assist Control Without Hill-Start Assist Control\nHILL-START ASSIST CONTROL (HAC)\n•  When the vehicle starts off on a steep or slippery hill, it may'), Document(metadata={'id': 'safety manual.pdf_p10_c3', 'source': 'safety manual.pdf', 'page_number': 10, 'start_line_number': 33, 'end_line_number': 41
    }, page_content='HILL-START ASSIST CONTROL (HAC)\n•  When the vehicle starts off on a steep or slippery hill, it may \nstart to descend backwards while the driver switches from \nthe brake pedal to the accelerator pedal, thus making it \ndifficult for the vehicle to start off. \n•  To help prevent this from occurring, the Hill-Start Assist \nControl temporarily (approximately 2 seconds at the \nmaximum) applies the brakes to all four wheels in order to \nhelp prevent the vehicle from descending backward.'), Document(metadata={'id': 'safety manual.pdf_p10_c4', 'source': 'safety manual.pdf', 'page_number': 10, 'start_line_number': 16, 'end_line_number': 75
    }, page_content='help prevent the vehicle from descending backward.\nWithout Load in Rear\nFront Brake Force\nIdeal Brake Force Distribution\nRear Brake\nForce\nEBD Control\nWith Load in Rear\nFront Brake Force\nIdeal Brake Force Distribution\nRear Brake\nForce\nEBD Control\nWithout Trailer Sway Control\nWith Trailer Sway Control\nSide Wind\nSide Wind Brake Control + Engine Output Control\nWith Hill-Start Assist Control Without Hill-Start Assist Control\nWithout Load in Rear\nFront Brake Force\nIdeal Brake Force Distribution'), Document(metadata={'id': 'safety manual.pdf_p10_c5', 'source': 'safety manual.pdf', 'page_number': 10, 'start_line_number': 16, 'end_line_number': 75
    }, page_content='Without Load in Rear\nFront Brake Force\nIdeal Brake Force Distribution\nRear Brake\nForce\nEBD Control\nWith Load in Rear\nFront Brake Force\nIdeal Brake Force Distribution\nRear Brake\nForce\nEBD Control\nWithout Trailer Sway Control\nWith Trailer Sway Control\nSide Wind\nSide Wind Brake Control + Engine Output Control\nWith Hill-Start Assist Control Without Hill-Start Assist Control'), Document(metadata={'id': 'safety manual.pdf_p11_c0', 'source': 'safety manual.pdf', 'page_number': 11, 'start_line_number': 1, 'end_line_number': 10
    }, page_content='11\nCAUTION WHEN DRIVING AND STOPPING\nFOR PEOPLE WHO USE ELECTRO-MEDICAL DEVICES\n•  People with implanted pacemakers, implanted cardiac \ndefibrillators or similar devices should be careful in handling \nthe smart entry or start system as it uses weak radio waves.\n•  The smart entry or start system can be disabled. Ask your  \nLexus / Toyota dealer for details.\nTHE DRIVER MUST CONTROL THE ELECTRONIC KEY\n•  When changing drivers, transfer the electronic key to the next'), Document(metadata={'id': 'safety manual.pdf_p11_c1', 'source': 'safety manual.pdf', 'page_number': 11, 'start_line_number': 10, 'end_line_number': 18
    }, page_content='•  When changing drivers, transfer the electronic key to the next \ndriver before leaving the driver’s seat. If you leave the vehicle \nwhile carrying the electronic key, the next driver will not be able \nto restart the engine.\nDRIVER DISTRACTION \n•  Do not be preoccupied with the screen of the navigation system \nor audio system while driving. Read the owner’s manual in \nadvance and make settings before driving.\nSET THE DRIVER’S SIDE FLOOR MAT CORRECTLY'), Document(metadata={'id': 'safety manual.pdf_p11_c2', 'source': 'safety manual.pdf', 'page_number': 11, 'start_line_number': 17, 'end_line_number': 26
    }, page_content='advance and make settings before driving.\nSET THE DRIVER’S SIDE FLOOR MAT CORRECTLY\n•  Use only the floor mat designed specifically for the driver’s side \nof the vehicle.\n•  Use the retaining clips provided to attach the floor mat securely \nin place onto the carpet where it does not interfere with the \naccelerator pedal.\n•  For details on how to attach the floor mat, refer to the installation  \ninstructions supplied with the floor mat.\n 13  SMART ENTRY AND START SYSTEM'), Document(metadata={'id': 'safety manual.pdf_p11_c3', 'source': 'safety manual.pdf', 'page_number': 11, 'start_line_number': 2, 'end_line_number': 27
    }, page_content='instructions supplied with the floor mat.\n 13  SMART ENTRY AND START SYSTEM  \n 14  CAUTION WHEN DRIVING AND STOPPING'), Document(metadata={'id': 'safety manual.pdf_p12_c0', 'source': 'safety manual.pdf', 'page_number': 12, 'start_line_number': 1, 'end_line_number': 31
    }, page_content='12  14  CAUTION WHEN DRIVING AND STOPPING\nSTEP 1 \nSteadily step on the brake pedal with \nboth feet and firmly depress it.\nSTEP 2 \nPosition the shift lever to N.\nSTEP 3 \nAfter slowing down, stop the vehicle in  \na safe place by the side of the road.\nSTEP 4 \nSwitch off the engine (or hybrid system).\nSTEP 5 \nRemove the floor mat.\n[If shift lever cannot be shifted to N
    ] \nSTEP 1 \nKeep depressing the brake pedal with both feet  \nto reduce vehicle speed as much as possible.\nSTEP 2A'), Document(metadata={'id': 'safety manual.pdf_p12_c1', 'source': 'safety manual.pdf', 'page_number': 12, 'start_line_number': 5, 'end_line_number': 32
    }, page_content='to reduce vehicle speed as much as possible.\nSTEP 2A  \nVehicles with a smart key system: Stop the \nengine (or hybrid system) by pressing and \nholding the “ENGINE START STOP (or POWER)” \nswitch for 3 consecutive seconds or more.\nSTEP 2B \nVehicles without a smart key system: Stop the \nengine by turning the engine switch to the \n“ACC” position. \nSTEP 3 \nStop the vehicle in a safe place by the side \nof the road.\nSTEP 4 \nRemove the floor mat.\nIF THE ACCELERATOR PEDAL IS CAUGHT UNDER THE'), Document(metadata={'id': 'safety manual.pdf_p12_c2', 'source': 'safety manual.pdf', 'page_number': 12, 'start_line_number': 10, 'end_line_number': 39
    }, page_content='of the road.\nSTEP 4 \nRemove the floor mat.\nIF THE ACCELERATOR PEDAL IS CAUGHT UNDER THE \nFLOOR MAT AND IS DIFFICULT TO DISENGAGE  \nSHIFT CHANGES\n•  Engage the shift lever in positions that are suitable for \nwhichever driving conditions apply. On a slope, do not let \nthe vehicle roll backward while the shift lever is in the driving \nposition, or roll forward while the shift is in R. Doing so may \ncause the engine to stall, resulting in severely diminished brake'), Document(metadata={'id': 'safety manual.pdf_p12_c3', 'source': 'safety manual.pdf', 'page_number': 12, 'start_line_number': 39, 'end_line_number': 41
    }, page_content='cause the engine to stall, resulting in severely diminished brake \nperformance and making the steering wheel extremely difficult \nto turn, which could result in a serious accident.'), Document(metadata={'id': 'safety manual.pdf_p13_c0', 'source': 'safety manual.pdf', 'page_number': 13, 'start_line_number': 1, 'end_line_number': 12
    }, page_content='13\nDANGER OF FIRE IF THE VEHICLE IS FLOODED OR SUBMERGED\n•  If water enters the engine compartment, the engine could be \ndamaged and the penetration of water into the electrical system \ncould result in a short circuit or fire.\n•  If the vehicle is submerged in a heavy rainfall, do not start the engine \nto avoid further damage. Push the vehicle by hand if you need to \nmove your vehicle. Request the dealer or road service for rescue.'), Document(metadata={'id': 'safety manual.pdf_p13_c1', 'source': 'safety manual.pdf', 'page_number': 13, 'start_line_number': 8, 'end_line_number': 77
    }, page_content='move your vehicle. Request the dealer or road service for rescue.\n•  Do not forcefully drive the vehicle on a flooded road even through \nshallow water. The water could splash upwards and get into the \nengine compartment.\nIF THE VEHICLE IS SUBMERGED, CALMLY EXIT THE VEHICLE\n•  Unbuckle your seatbelt.\n•  If the volume of water does not prevent you from opening the door, \nopen the door and immediately exit the vehicle.\n•  If you are unable to open the door, climb out through the window.'), Document(metadata={'id': 'safety manual.pdf_p13_c2', 'source': 'safety manual.pdf', 'page_number': 13, 'start_line_number': 16, 'end_line_number': 23
    }, page_content='•  If you are unable to open the door, climb out through the window. \nIf the window cannot be lowered, break the glass and carefully \nclimb out. Do not attempt to break the windshield to escape vehicle.\n•  If you are unable to break the window, wait until the vehicle is \nflooded to the level that there is no difference in water pressure \nbetween the inside and outside of the vehicle, then immediately \nexit through the door.\nTHIS SAFETY GUIDEBOOK IS COMMON TO ALL VEHICLES'), Document(metadata={'id': 'safety manual.pdf_p13_c3', 'source': 'safety manual.pdf', 'page_number': 13, 'start_line_number': 22, 'end_line_number': 96
    }, page_content='exit through the door.\nTHIS SAFETY GUIDEBOOK IS COMMON TO ALL VEHICLES\n•  There are specific cautions for hybrid vehicles such as those on \nhigh voltage parts. For cautions specific to each vehicle, refer  \nto the owner’s manual for your vehicle.\n 14  CAUTION WHEN DRIVING AND STOPPING\nBRAKE\nFORCE\nBRAKE\nFORCE\nWithout VSC\nWithout Brake Assist\nWithout ABS\nWith ABS\nBraking Point\nWith Brake Assist\nWithout VSC\nWith VSC\nBA\nWithout TRC With TRC\nWithout VSC\nFront wheel slipping\nSteering loses control'), Document(metadata={'id': 'safety manual.pdf_p13_c4', 'source': 'safety manual.pdf', 'page_number': 13, 'start_line_number': 28, 'end_line_number': 96
    }, page_content='With VSC\nBA\nWithout TRC With TRC\nWithout VSC\nFront wheel slipping\nSteering loses control\nWithout VSC\nRear wheel slipping\nOver-steering\nWith VSC\nWith ABS\nWithout ABS\nBRAKE\nFORCE\nBRAKE\nFORCE\nWithout VSC\nWithout Brake Assist\nWithout ABS\nWith ABS\nBraking Point\nWith Brake Assist\nWithout VSC\nWith VSC\nBA\nWithout TRC With TRC\nWithout VSC\nFront wheel slipping\nSteering loses control\nWithout VSC\nRear wheel slipping\nOver-steering\nWith VSC\nWith ABS\nWithout ABS\nBRAKE\nFORCE\nBRAKE\nFORCE\nWithout VSC'), Document(metadata={'id': 'safety manual.pdf_p13_c5', 'source': 'safety manual.pdf', 'page_number': 13, 'start_line_number': 28, 'end_line_number': 96
    }, page_content='Rear wheel slipping\nOver-steering\nWith VSC\nWith ABS\nWithout ABS\nBRAKE\nFORCE\nBRAKE\nFORCE\nWithout VSC\nWithout Brake Assist\nWithout ABS\nWith ABS\nBraking Point\nWith Brake Assist\nWithout VSC\nWith VSC\nBA\nWithout TRC With TRC\nWithout VSC\nFront wheel slipping\nSteering loses control\nWithout VSC\nRear wheel slipping\nOver-steering\nWith VSC\nWith ABS\nWithout ABS'), Document(metadata={'id': 'safety manual.pdf_p14_c0', 'source': 'safety manual.pdf', 'page_number': 14, 'start_line_number': 1, 'end_line_number': 8
    }, page_content='14\nBUKU PANDUAN KESELAMATAN INI MENERANGKAN SECARA RINGKAS OPERASI \nKENDERAAN ANDA DAN BEBERAPA CIRI KESELAMATAN UTAMA. \nSILA MAKLUM BAHAWA MANUAL INI DIGUNAKAN UNTUK SEMUA MODEL DAN \nMENERANGKAN SEMUA PERALATAN, TERMASUKLAH YANG BERSIFAT PILIHAN. \nOLEH ITU, ANDA MUNGKIN MENDAPATI BEBERAPA PENERANGAN UNTUK \nPERALATAN YANG TIDAK DIPASANG PADA KENDERAAN ANDA.\nPEMANDU BERTANGGUNGJAWAB UNTUK MEMANDU KENDERAAAN DENGAN'), Document(metadata={'id': 'safety manual.pdf_p14_c1', 'source': 'safety manual.pdf', 'page_number': 14, 'start_line_number': 8, 'end_line_number': 27
    }, page_content='PEMANDU BERTANGGUNGJAWAB UNTUK MEMANDU KENDERAAAN DENGAN              \nSELAMAT. FUNGSI KESELAMATAN DALAM KENDERAAN ANDA ADALAH SEBAGAI       \nTAMBAHAN SAHAJA. SENTIASA MEMERHATIKAN PERSEKITARAN ANDA.\nmuka surat 15 \n 01  TALI PINGGANG KELEDAR\nmuka surat 16–17 \n 02  KESELAMATAN KANAK-KANAK\nmuka surat 18-19 \n 03  BEG UDARA SRS\nmuka surat 19 \n 04  ABS (SISTEM BREK ANTIKUNCI)\nmuka surat 20 \n 05  BANTUAN BREK\nmuka surat 20 \n 06  VSC (SISTEM KAWALAN KESTABILAN KENDERAAN)\nmuka surat 21'), Document(metadata={'id': 'safety manual.pdf_p14_c2', 'source': 'safety manual.pdf', 'page_number': 14, 'start_line_number': 1, 'end_line_number': 41
    }, page_content='05  BANTUAN BREK\nmuka surat 20 \n 06  VSC (SISTEM KAWALAN KESTABILAN KENDERAAN)\nmuka surat 21 \n 07  ELECTRONIC BRAKE FORCE DISTRIBUTION\nmuka surat 21 \n 08  EMERGENCY BRAKE SIGNAL\nmuka surat 21 \n 09  BRAKE OVERRIDE SYSTEM\nmuka surat 22  \n 10  TRAILER SWAY CONTROL\nmuka surat 22  \n 11  BLIND SPOT MONITORING & REAR CROSS TRAFFIC ALERT\nmuka surat 22  \n 12  HILL ASSIST\nmuka surat 23 \n 13  SISTEM PINTAR MULA DAN MASUK\nmuka surat 23–25 \n 14  BERHATI-HATI SEMASA MEMANDU DAN BERHENTI \n \n  \nKANDUNGAN'), Document(metadata={'id': 'safety manual.pdf_p15_c0', 'source': 'safety manual.pdf', 'page_number': 15, 'start_line_number': 1, 'end_line_number': 13
    }, page_content='15\nCara memakai tali pinggang keledar dengan betul \nSemua penumpang di dalam kenderaan perlulah mengancing  \ntali pinggang keledar mereka sepanjang masa.\nDUDUK DENGAN POSISI BADAN YANG BETUL\n•  Tegakkan kedudukan kerusi dan sandarkan belakang anda pada \nsandaran kerusi.\n•  Elakkan daripada merebahkan sandaran kerusi. Jika kerusi anda \ndirebahkan semasa kemalangan, anda mungkin tergelongsor \ndi bawah tali pinggang keledar – yang boleh menyebabkan \nkecederaan serius atau mengancam nyawa.'), Document(metadata={'id': 'safety manual.pdf_p15_c1', 'source': 'safety manual.pdf', 'page_number': 15, 'start_line_number': 10, 'end_line_number': 18
    }, page_content='di bawah tali pinggang keledar – yang boleh menyebabkan \nkecederaan serius atau mengancam nyawa.\nKANCINGKAN TALI PINGGANG KELEDAR ANDA \nDENGAN BETUL\n•  Betulkan kedudukan tali pinggang bahu supaya ia tidak \nbersentuhan dengan leher atau tergelongsor daripada bahu anda.\n•  Betulkan kedudukan tali pinggang di antara pelvis dan abdomen.\n• Pastikan kancing tali pinggang keledar dipasang rapi di tempatnya.\n•  Baca selanjutnya tentang keselamatan tali pinggang keledar untuk'), Document(metadata={'id': 'safety manual.pdf_p15_c2', 'source': 'safety manual.pdf', 'page_number': 15, 'start_line_number': 18, 'end_line_number': 23
    }, page_content='•  Baca selanjutnya tentang keselamatan tali pinggang keledar untuk  \nkanak-kanak di bawah ‘2 Keselamatan Kanak-kanak’ dalam  \nBuku Panduan Keselamatan ini.\nUntuk arahan tentang cara melaraskan tali pinggang keledar,  \nsila rujuk manual pemilik untuk kenderaan anda.\n 01  TALI PINGGANG KELEDAR'), Document(metadata={'id': 'safety manual.pdf_p16_c0', 'source': 'safety manual.pdf', 'page_number': 16, 'start_line_number': 1, 'end_line_number': 9
    }, page_content='16\nJANGAN BENARKAN KANAK-KANAK BERMAIN DENGAN BAHAGIAN KENDERAAN  \nYANG BOLEH BUKA DAN TUTUP\n•  Elakkan kanak-kanak daripada bermain dengan pintu atau tingkap kerana ia boleh menyebabkan \nkecederaan atau kemalangan.\nMEMANDU APABILA BERSAMA-SAMA DENGAN KANAK-KANAK\n•  Kanak-kanak mestilah duduk di kerusi belakang.\n•  Penumpang dewasa mestilah duduk di sebelah atau berdekatan dengan kanak-kanak  \nuntuk memastikan keselamatan mereka terjamin.'), Document(metadata={'id': 'safety manual.pdf_p16_c1', 'source': 'safety manual.pdf', 'page_number': 16, 'start_line_number': 2, 'end_line_number': 31
    }, page_content='untuk memastikan keselamatan mereka terjamin.\n•  Sentiasa ikuti arahan pengilang apabila menggunakan sistem sekatan kanak-kanak. \n 02  KESELAMATAN KANAK-KANAK\nDUDUKKAN KANAK-KANAK DALAM KEADAAN YANG BETUL\n•  Jangan benarkan kanak-kanak berdiri atau berlutut di atas kerusi \npenumpang depan, atau duduk di atas riba penumpang depan. \nBeg udara penumpang depan SRS boleh mengembung dengan \nkelajuan dan daya yang tinggi.\n•  Apabila menggunakan sistem sekatan kanak-kanak, sila pastikan'), Document(metadata={'id': 'safety manual.pdf_p16_c2', 'source': 'safety manual.pdf', 'page_number': 16, 'start_line_number': 16, 'end_line_number': 31
    }, page_content='kelajuan dan daya yang tinggi.\n•  Apabila menggunakan sistem sekatan kanak-kanak, sila pastikan \nkepala kanak-kanak atau bahagian badan yang lain tidak bersandar \npada pintu, kerusi, tiang depan, tiang belakang atau rel tepi bumbung.\nMEMASANG SISTEM SEKATAN KANAK-KANAK\n•  Sistem sekatan kanak-kanak mestilah dipasang pada kerusi luar \nbahagian belakang dengan mengikuti arahan yang disediakan  \noleh pengilang.\n•  Apabila menggunakan bar khas untuk mengikat kerusi kanak-kanak'), Document(metadata={'id': 'safety manual.pdf_p16_c3', 'source': 'safety manual.pdf', 'page_number': 16, 'start_line_number': 16, 'end_line_number': 31
    }, page_content='oleh pengilang.\n•  Apabila menggunakan bar khas untuk mengikat kerusi kanak-kanak \nyang menyokong ISOFIX, periksa tiada halangan di kawasan sekitar \ndan tali pinggang keledar tidak tersekat.\n•  Sistem sekatan kanak-kanak yang menghadap ke hadapan mestilah \ndipasang pada kerusi penumpang depan apabila diperlukan. \nSentiasa gerakkan kerusi sejauh yang boleh ke belakang kerana beg \nudara penumpang depan boleh mengembung dengan kelajuan dan \ndaya yang tinggi.'), Document(metadata={'id': 'safety manual.pdf_p17_c0', 'source': 'safety manual.pdf', 'page_number': 17, 'start_line_number': 1, 'end_line_number': 11
    }, page_content='17\nSila rujuk amaran dengan kandungan yang sama yang dipaparkan  \npada pelindung matahari di bahagian kerusi penumpang.\n•  Jangan sesekali memasang sistem sekatan kanak-kanak yang \nmenghadap ke belakang di kerusi penumpang depan.\n•  Apabila menggunakan kerusi kanak-kanak, sentiasa pastikan  \nbahawa tali pinggang bahu diletakkan merentasi bahagian tengah \nbahu anak anda.\n \nJANGAN BENARKAN KANAK-KANAK BERMAIN DENGAN  \nTALI PINGGANG KELEDAR'), Document(metadata={'id': 'safety manual.pdf_p17_c1', 'source': 'safety manual.pdf', 'page_number': 17, 'start_line_number': 8, 'end_line_number': 18
    }, page_content='bahu anak anda.\n \nJANGAN BENARKAN KANAK-KANAK BERMAIN DENGAN  \nTALI PINGGANG KELEDAR\n•  Jika tali kekang ditarik hingga ke hujung, ALR (Automatic Locking \nRetractor – Retraktor Pengunci Automatik) akan diaktifkan dan  \ntali pinggang keledar tidak boleh dilonggarkan.\n•  Jika tali pinggang keledar terpintal di sekeliling leher kanak-kanak, \nia boleh membawa maut kerana tercekik. Jika kancing tidak boleh \ndibuka, gunakan gunting atau alat tajam yang lain untuk menggunting \ntali pinggang keledar.'), Document(metadata={'id': 'safety manual.pdf_p17_c2', 'source': 'safety manual.pdf', 'page_number': 17, 'start_line_number': 11, 'end_line_number': 26
    }, page_content='dibuka, gunakan gunting atau alat tajam yang lain untuk menggunting \ntali pinggang keledar.\nPERALATAN UNTUK MENGELAKKAN BAHAYA DISEBABKAN \nOLEH OPERASI YANG SALAH DARIPADA KANAK-KANAK \n•  Pengunci pintu pelindung kanak-kanak Peranti ini mengelakkan \nkanak-kanak daripada membuka pintu kerusi belakang dari dalam.\n•  Suis kunci tingkap \nPeranti ini mengelakkan kanak-kanak daripada mengendalikan tingkap.  \nJANGAN SEKALI-KALI MEMBIARKAN KANAK-KANAK  \nTANPA PENGAWASAN DI DALAM KENDERAAN'), Document(metadata={'id': 'safety manual.pdf_p17_c3', 'source': 'safety manual.pdf', 'page_number': 17, 'start_line_number': 25, 'end_line_number': 32
    }, page_content='JANGAN SEKALI-KALI MEMBIARKAN KANAK-KANAK  \nTANPA PENGAWASAN DI DALAM KENDERAAN\n•  Suhu di dalam kenderaan yang diletakkan di bawah cahaya matahari \nboleh menjadi sangat panas dan kanak-kanak boleh mengalami \nstrok haba dan penyahhidratan yang boleh membawa maut. Selain \nitu, kanak-kanak juga boleh terlibat dalam kemalangan yang tidak \ndijangka jika bermain dengan kawalan dan peralatan kenderaan.\n 02  KESELAMATAN KANAK-KANAK'), Document(metadata={'id': 'safety manual.pdf_p18_c0', 'source': 'safety manual.pdf', 'page_number': 18, 'start_line_number': 1, 'end_line_number': 28
    }, page_content='18\nBeg udara SRS \nBeg udara SRS (Supplemental Restraint System – \nSistem Sekatan Tambahan) direka untuk memberikan \nperlindungan tambahan kepada pemandu dan penumpang \nselain perlindungan keselamatan utama yang diberikan oleh \ntali pinggang keledar. Jenis-jenis beg udara SRS adalah  \nseperti di bawah:\n 1 Beg udara pemandu / Beg udara penumpang depan SRS \n2 Beg udara sisi SRS\nSPESIFIKASI MUNGKIN BERBEZA DARIPADA MODEL YANG TERSEDIA.\nPERLANGGARAN DEPAN PADA  \nKELAJUAN RENDAH'), Document(metadata={'id': 'safety manual.pdf_p18_c1', 'source': 'safety manual.pdf', 'page_number': 18, 'start_line_number': 2, 'end_line_number': 29
    }, page_content='SPESIFIKASI MUNGKIN BERBEZA DARIPADA MODEL YANG TERSEDIA.\nPERLANGGARAN DEPAN PADA  \nKELAJUAN RENDAH\nPERLANGGARAN DARI SUDUT PERLANGGARAN DENGAN POKOK YANG \nKECIL ATAU OBJEK LAIN YANG SECARA \nRELATIFNYA BOLEH DIALIHKAN\nPERLANGGARAN DI MANA DAYA \nPERLANGGARANNYA KE ARAH BAWAH \nSEPERTI IMPAK DENGAN PLATFORM \nMUATAN LORI\nPERLANGGARAN YANG IMPAKNYA \nDATANG DARI SUDUT\nPERLANGGARAN DI MANA RUANG \nPENUMPANG TIDAK TERKENA IMPAK TERUS\n 03  BEG UDARA SRS \n1\n12\n2\nDUDUK DENGAN POSTUR BADAN YANG BETUL'), Document(metadata={'id': 'safety manual.pdf_p18_c2', 'source': 'safety manual.pdf', 'page_number': 18, 'start_line_number': 2, 'end_line_number': 37
    }, page_content='PENUMPANG TIDAK TERKENA IMPAK TERUS\n 03  BEG UDARA SRS \n1\n12\n2\nDUDUK DENGAN POSTUR BADAN YANG BETUL\n•  Jangan duduk terlalu dekat dengan stereng atau papan pemuka. \nPemandu atau penumpang depan tidak sepatutnya memangku \nbarang di atas riba mereka.\n•  Jangan benarkan sesiapa bersandar pada pintu, tiang tengah,  \ntiang belakang dan rel tepi bumbung.\n•  Jangan benarkan sesiapa berlutut di atas kerusi penumpang \nmenghadap pintu tepi, meletakkan kepala atau tangan mereka \nke luar tingkap.'), Document(metadata={'id': 'safety manual.pdf_p18_c3', 'source': 'safety manual.pdf', 'page_number': 18, 'start_line_number': 2, 'end_line_number': 41
    }, page_content='menghadap pintu tepi, meletakkan kepala atau tangan mereka \nke luar tingkap.\nBEG UDARA SRS MUNGKIN TIDAK BEROPERASI WALAUPUN \nSEMASA PERLANGGARAN\n•  Contoh beg udara SRS tidak beroperasi (kenderaan ujian) \nBeg udara pemandu dan penumpang depan SRS'), Document(metadata={'id': 'safety manual.pdf_p19_c0', 'source': 'safety manual.pdf', 'page_number': 19, 'start_line_number': 1, 'end_line_number': 63
    }, page_content='19\n•  Contoh kedudukan yang beg udara SRS mungkin tidak  \nakan menunjukkan keberkesanan utamanya.\nAPABILA BERGULING ATAU TERBALIK  \nUntuk keterangan lanjut, sila rujuk manual pemilik untuk \nkenderaan anda.\nJANGAN MEMASANG OBJEK DI SEKITAR BEG UDARA SRS\n•  Jangan pasang objek di kawasan seperti papan pemuka, pad \nstereng, bahagian bawah panel alatan, pintu, cermin depan, tiang \ndepan atau belakang, rel tepi bumbung dan cengkaman bantu.\nABS'), Document(metadata={'id': 'safety manual.pdf_p19_c1', 'source': 'safety manual.pdf', 'page_number': 19, 'start_line_number': 10, 'end_line_number': 63
    }, page_content='depan atau belakang, rel tepi bumbung dan cengkaman bantu.\nABS \nABS (Anti-locking Braking System – Sistem Brek Antikunci) mengelakkan roda daripada terkunci, \nmembolehkan pemandu terus mengawal kenderaan dalam situasi pembrekan kecemasan. \n•  Jika pembrekan mengejut diperlukan, tekan dengan kuat  \npada pedal brek.\n•  Jangan mengepam atau melepaskan pedal brek.\n•  Anda akan merasakan gegaran kecil pada pedal brek dan mendengar \nbunyi bising – ini menandakan bahawa ABS sedang aktif.'), Document(metadata={'id': 'safety manual.pdf_p19_c2', 'source': 'safety manual.pdf', 'page_number': 19, 'start_line_number': 11, 'end_line_number': 63
    }, page_content='bunyi bising – ini menandakan bahawa ABS sedang aktif.\nABS TIDAK AKAN MEMENDEKKAN JARAK PEMBREKAN\n•  Kenderaan ABS mungkin mengambil masa yang agak lama \nuntuk berhenti di atas jalan berkeadaan teruk; seperti jalan yang \nberbonggol-bonggol, berturap batu atau tidak rata.\nPeringatan: ABS tidak menyingkirkan bahaya kemalangan. Oleh itu, \npastikan anda memandu dengan selamat dan kekalkan jarak yang \nselamat dari kenderaan di hadapan anda.\n 03  BEG UDARA SRS  \n 04  ABS\nBRAKE\nFORCE\nBRAKE\nFORCE'), Document(metadata={'id': 'safety manual.pdf_p19_c3', 'source': 'safety manual.pdf', 'page_number': 19, 'start_line_number': 11, 'end_line_number': 73
    }, page_content='selamat dari kenderaan di hadapan anda.\n 03  BEG UDARA SRS  \n 04  ABS\nBRAKE\nFORCE\nBRAKE\nFORCE\nWithout VSC\nTanpa Bantuan Brek\nWithout ABS\nWith ABS\nBraking Point\nDengan Bantuan Brek\nWithout VSC\nWith VSC\nBA\nTanpa TRC Dengan TRC\nTanpa VSC\nRoda depan tergelincir\nHilang kawalan stereng\nTanpa VSC\nRoda belakang tergelincir\nTerlebih pusing\nDengan VSC\nDengan ABS\nTanpa ABS\nBRAKE\nFORCE\nBRAKE\nFORCE\nWithout VSC\nWithout Brake Assist\nWithout ABS\nWith ABS\nBraking Point\nWith Brake Assist\nWithout VSC\nWith VSC\nBA'), Document(metadata={'id': 'safety manual.pdf_p19_c4', 'source': 'safety manual.pdf', 'page_number': 19, 'start_line_number': 11, 'end_line_number': 73
    }, page_content='Without Brake Assist\nWithout ABS\nWith ABS\nBraking Point\nWith Brake Assist\nWithout VSC\nWith VSC\nBA\nWithout TRC With TRC\nWithout VSC\nFront wheel slipping\nSteering loses control\nWithout VSC\nRear wheel slipping\nOver-steering\nWith VSC\nWith ABS\nWithout ABS'), Document(metadata={'id': 'safety manual.pdf_p20_c0', 'source': 'safety manual.pdf', 'page_number': 20, 'start_line_number': 1, 'end_line_number': 59
    }, page_content='20\nBANTUAN BREK \nBantuan Brek membantu dalam situasi kecemasan apabila tekanan pada \npedal brek tidak mencukupi semasa pembrekan mengejut atau ‘panik’\nVSC (Vehicle Stability Control system – \nSistem Kawalan Kestabilan Kenderaan) \nSistem VSC (Vehicle Stability Control – Kawalan Kestabilan Kenderaan) membantu mengelakkan \nkegelinciran roda semasa membelokkan kenderaan atau semasa situasi pengemudian mengejut.'), Document(metadata={'id': 'safety manual.pdf_p20_c1', 'source': 'safety manual.pdf', 'page_number': 20, 'start_line_number': 2, 'end_line_number': 59
    }, page_content='kegelinciran roda semasa membelokkan kenderaan atau semasa situasi pengemudian mengejut.\n•  Bantuan Brek membantu memberikan daya brek yang penuh apabila ia mengesan tekanan yang \ndikenakan pada pedal brek tidak mencukupi.\n•  Sistem komputer menganalisis sama ada perlu atau tidak mengaktifkan Bantuan Brek ber dasarkan \nsecepat mana dan sekuat mana pemandu menekan pedal brek.\n•  Sistem mengesan ketidakstabilan kenderaan dan mengawal kegelongsoran, membolehkan'), Document(metadata={'id': 'safety manual.pdf_p20_c2', 'source': 'safety manual.pdf', 'page_number': 20, 'start_line_number': 2, 'end_line_number': 59
    }, page_content='•  Sistem mengesan ketidakstabilan kenderaan dan mengawal kegelongsoran, membolehkan \npemandu untuk terus mengawal kenderaan.\n \nIlustrasi menunjukkan apa yang berlaku pada kereta selepas pemandu memutar stereng \ndengan cepat di pertengahan belokan. Dengan bantuan VSC, kereta dikendalikan dengan \nbetul dan dapat kembali ke lorongnya yang asal dengan cepat.\nPeringatan: VSC tidak menyingkirkan bahaya kemalangan. Ia hanya membantu dengan \nkestabilan kenderaan\n 05  BANTUAN BREK'), Document(metadata={'id': 'safety manual.pdf_p20_c3', 'source': 'safety manual.pdf', 'page_number': 20, 'start_line_number': 2, 'end_line_number': 69
    }, page_content='kestabilan kenderaan\n 05  BANTUAN BREK \n 06  VSC (VEHICLE STABILITY CONTROL SYSTEM – SISTEM \nKAWALAN KESTABILAN KENDERAAN) \nBRAKE\nFORCE\nBRAKE\nFORCE\nWithout VSC\nTanpa Bantuan Brek\nWithout ABS\nWith ABS\nBraking Point\nDengan Bantuan Brek\nWithout VSC\nWith VSC\nBA\nTanpa TRC Dengan TRC\nTanpa VSC\nRoda depan tergelincir\nHilang kawalan stereng\nTanpa VSC\nRoda belakang tergelincir\nTerlebih pusing\nDengan VSC\nDengan ABS\nTanpa ABS\nBRAKE\nFORCE\nBRAKE\nFORCE\nWithout VSC\nTanpa Bantuan Brek\nWithout ABS\nWith ABS'), Document(metadata={'id': 'safety manual.pdf_p20_c4', 'source': 'safety manual.pdf', 'page_number': 20, 'start_line_number': 2, 'end_line_number': 69
    }, page_content='Dengan ABS\nTanpa ABS\nBRAKE\nFORCE\nBRAKE\nFORCE\nWithout VSC\nTanpa Bantuan Brek\nWithout ABS\nWith ABS\nBraking Point\nDengan Bantuan Brek\nWithout VSC\nWith VSC\nBA\nTanpa TRC Dengan TRC\nTanpa VSC\nRoda depan tergelincir\nHilang kawalan stereng\nTanpa VSC\nRoda belakang tergelincir\nTerlebih pusing\nDengan VSC\nDengan ABS\nTanpa ABS'), Document(metadata={'id': 'safety manual.pdf_p21_c0', 'source': 'safety manual.pdf', 'page_number': 21, 'start_line_number': 1, 'end_line_number': 8
    }, page_content='21\n•  Fungsi ini juga mengawal kuasa brek semasa membelok kenderaan pada roda-roda mengikut \nkeadaan kenderaan pada masa itu. Ini memastikan kestabilan kenderaan dan brek prestasi yang \nbaik. \nEMERGENCY BRAKE SIGNAL\n•  Emergency Brake Signal akan menyalakan lampu amaran hazard secara automatik sekiranya       \nterdapat keadaan brek kecemasan untuk mengurangkan risiko dilanggar dari belakang.\n•  Skid Control ECU akan mengesan keadaan kenderaan dan brek dengan menggunakan pengesan'), Document(metadata={'id': 'safety manual.pdf_p21_c1', 'source': 'safety manual.pdf', 'page_number': 21, 'start_line_number': 8, 'end_line_number': 28
    }, page_content='•  Skid Control ECU akan mengesan keadaan kenderaan dan brek dengan menggunakan pengesan \nkelajuan dan stop light switch assembly.\n•  Sekiranya brek kecemasan dikesan berdasarkan keadaan di atas, skid control ECU akan menghan -\ntar isyarat kepada combination meter assembly untuk menyalakan lampu amaran hazard.\nBRAKE OVERRIDE SYSTEM\n•  Apabila kedua-dua pedal accelerator and brek tertekan, sistem ini boleh mengawal enjin output \ndan prestasi brek.\n 07  ELECTRONIC BRAKE FORCE DISTRIBUTION'), Document(metadata={'id': 'safety manual.pdf_p21_c2', 'source': 'safety manual.pdf', 'page_number': 21, 'start_line_number': 5, 'end_line_number': 35
    }, page_content='dan prestasi brek.\n 07  ELECTRONIC BRAKE FORCE DISTRIBUTION  \n 08  EMERGENCY BRAKE SIGNAL\n09  BRAKE OVERRIDE SYSTEM\nWithout Load in Rear\nFront Brake Force\nIdeal Brake Force Distribution\nRear Brake\nForce\nEBD Control\nWith Load in Rear\nFront Brake Force\nIdeal Brake Force Distribution\nRear Brake\nForce\nEBD Control\nWithout Trailer Sway Control\nWith Trailer Sway Control\nSide Wind\nSide Wind Brake Control + Engine Output Control\nWith Hill-Start Assist Control Without Hill-Start Assist Control'), Document(metadata={'id': 'safety manual.pdf_p21_c3', 'source': 'safety manual.pdf', 'page_number': 21, 'start_line_number': 4, 'end_line_number': 37
    }, page_content='With Hill-Start Assist Control Without Hill-Start Assist Control\nElectronic Brake Force Distribution (EBD)  \nEBD mengawal kuasa brek yang bertindak pada roda belakang mengikut perubahan \ndalam keadaan kenderaan untuk memastikan prestasi brek yang baik.'), Document(metadata={'id': 'safety manual.pdf_p22_c0', 'source': 'safety manual.pdf', 'page_number': 22, 'start_line_number': 1, 'end_line_number': 7
    }, page_content='22\n• Trailer Sway Control berfungsi untuk menstabilkan kenderaan apabila ia ditunda.\n•  Trailer Sway Control adalah sebahagian daripada fungsi VSC. Oleh itu, jika fungsi VSC dipadamkan \nTrailer Sway Control tidak akan beroperasi.\nBLIND SPOT MONITORING / REAR CROSS TRAFFIC ALERT\n•  Blind Spot Monitor System melaksanakan dua fungsi dengan menggunakan sensor-sensor yang \nsama: Blind Spot Monitor dan Rear Cross Traffic Alert.'), Document(metadata={'id': 'safety manual.pdf_p22_c1', 'source': 'safety manual.pdf', 'page_number': 22, 'start_line_number': 6, 'end_line_number': 15
    }, page_content='sama: Blind Spot Monitor dan Rear Cross Traffic Alert.\n•  Blind Spot Monitor System menggunakan sensor untuk mengesan kenderaan yang berada \ndi “blind spot” dan membantu pemandu untuk mengesahkan bahawa tiada kenderaan yang \nmenghalang ketika ingin menukar jalan.\n•  Fungsi Rear Cross Traffic Alert adalah untuk mengesan kenderaan di belakang semasa mengundur \nkenderaan.\n 10  TRAILER SWAY CONTROL \n 11  BLIND SPOT MONITORING & REAR CROSS TRAFFIC ALERT \n12  HILL ASSIST'), Document(metadata={'id': 'safety manual.pdf_p22_c2', 'source': 'safety manual.pdf', 'page_number': 22, 'start_line_number': 13, 'end_line_number': 23
    }, page_content='10  TRAILER SWAY CONTROL \n 11  BLIND SPOT MONITORING & REAR CROSS TRAFFIC ALERT \n12  HILL ASSIST\nHILL-START ASSIST CONTROL (HAC)\n•  Apabila pemandu ingin mengerakkan kenderaan ke hadapan \ndi atas bukit yang curam atau licin, kenderaan mungkin \nmengundur semasa pemandu beralih daripada pedal brek ke \npedal pemecut.\n•  Untuk mengelakkan keadaan ini daripada berlaku, Hill-\nStart Assist Control akan memasangkan brek kepada \nkeempat-empat roda kenderaan tersebut (lebih kurang 2'), Document(metadata={'id': 'safety manual.pdf_p22_c3', 'source': 'safety manual.pdf', 'page_number': 22, 'start_line_number': 23, 'end_line_number': 76
    }, page_content='keempat-empat roda kenderaan tersebut (lebih kurang 2 \nsaat maksimum) untuk mengelakkan kenderaan daripada \nmengundur ke belakang.\nWithout Load in Rear\nFront Brake Force\nIdeal Brake Force Distribution\nRear Brake\nForce\nEBD Control\nWith Load in Rear\nFront Brake Force\nIdeal Brake Force Distribution\nRear Brake\nForce\nEBD Control\nTanpa Trailer Sway Control\nDengan Trailer Sway Control\nAngin\nAngin Brake Control + Engine Output Control\nDengan Hill-Start Assist Control Tanpa Hill-Start Assist Control'), Document(metadata={'id': 'safety manual.pdf_p22_c4', 'source': 'safety manual.pdf', 'page_number': 22, 'start_line_number': 16, 'end_line_number': 76
    }, page_content='Dengan Hill-Start Assist Control Tanpa Hill-Start Assist Control\nWithout Load in Rear\nFront Brake Force\nIdeal Brake Force Distribution\nRear Brake\nForce\nEBD Control\nWith Load in Rear\nFront Brake Force\nIdeal Brake Force Distribution\nRear Brake\nForce\nEBD Control\nTanpa Trailer Sway Control\nDengan Trailer Sway Control\nAngin\nAngin Brake Control + Engine Output Control\nDengan Hill-Start Assist Control Tanpa Hill-Start Assist Control\nWithout Load in Rear\nFront Brake Force\nIdeal Brake Force Distribution'), Document(metadata={'id': 'safety manual.pdf_p22_c5', 'source': 'safety manual.pdf', 'page_number': 22, 'start_line_number': 26, 'end_line_number': 76
    }, page_content='Without Load in Rear\nFront Brake Force\nIdeal Brake Force Distribution\nRear Brake\nForce\nEBD Control\nWith Load in Rear\nFront Brake Force\nIdeal Brake Force Distribution\nRear Brake\nForce\nEBD Control\nTanpa Trailer Sway Control\nDengan Trailer Sway Control\nAngin\nAngin Brake Control + Engine Output Control\nDengan Hill-Start Assist Control Tanpa Hill-Start Assist Control'), Document(metadata={'id': 'safety manual.pdf_p23_c0', 'source': 'safety manual.pdf', 'page_number': 23, 'start_line_number': 1, 'end_line_number': 10
    }, page_content='23\nBERHATI-HATI SEMASA MEMANDU DAN BERHENTI \nUNTUK MEREKA YANG MENGGUNAKAN PERANTI \nELEKTRO-PERUBATAN\n•  Individu yang mempunyai implan perentak jantung, implan \npendefibril kardium atau peranti yang serupa dengannya mestilah \nberhati-hati semasa mengendalikan sistem pintar mula atau masuk \nkerana ia menggunakan gelombang radio yang lemah.\n•  Sistem pintar mula atau masuk boleh dinyahdayakan. Hubungi wakil \npenjual Lexus / Toyota anda untuk mendapatkan keterangan lanjut.'), Document(metadata={'id': 'safety manual.pdf_p23_c1', 'source': 'safety manual.pdf', 'page_number': 23, 'start_line_number': 10, 'end_line_number': 18
    }, page_content='penjual Lexus / Toyota anda untuk mendapatkan keterangan lanjut.\nPEMANDU MESTILAH MENGAWAL KUNCI ELEKTRONIK\n•  Semasa menukar pemandu, pindahkan kunci elektronik kepada \npemandu seterusnya sebelum meninggalkan kerusi pemandu. Jika \nanda meninggalkan kenderaan semasa membawa kunci elektronik, \npemandu seterusnya tidak akan dapat menghidupkan semula enjin.\nGANGGUAN PEMANDUAN  \n•  Jangan leka dengan skrin sistem navigasi atau sistem audio \nsemasa memandu.  Bacalah manual pemilik terlebih dahulu'), Document(metadata={'id': 'safety manual.pdf_p23_c2', 'source': 'safety manual.pdf', 'page_number': 23, 'start_line_number': 18, 'end_line_number': 27
    }, page_content='semasa memandu.  Bacalah manual pemilik terlebih dahulu  \ndan buatlah penetapan sebelum memandu.\nLETAKKAN ALAS KAKI BAHAGIAN PEMANDU \nDENGAN BETUL\n•  Gunakan alas kaki yang direka khusus untuk bahagian pemandu \nsahaja di dalam kenderaan.\n•  Gunakan klip penahan yang disediakan untuk memasang alas kaki  \ndengan rapi di tempatnya pada karpet iaitu di tempat yang tidak \nmengganggu pedal pemecut.\n•  Untuk keterangan lanjut tentang cara memasang alas kaki,'), Document(metadata={'id': 'safety manual.pdf_p23_c3', 'source': 'safety manual.pdf', 'page_number': 23, 'start_line_number': 2, 'end_line_number': 31
    }, page_content='mengganggu pedal pemecut.\n•  Untuk keterangan lanjut tentang cara memasang alas kaki, \nrujuklah arahan pemasangan yang disertakan bersama-sama \ndengan alas kaki.\n 13  SISTEM PINTAR MULA DAN MASUK   \n 14  BERHATI-HATI SEMASA MEMANDU DAN BERHENTI'), Document(metadata={'id': 'safety manual.pdf_p24_c0', 'source': 'safety manual.pdf', 'page_number': 24, 'start_line_number': 1, 'end_line_number': 31
    }, page_content='24  14  BERHATI-HATI SEMASA MEMANDU DAN BERHENTI \nLANGKAH 1  \nLetakkan kedua-dua belah kaki pada \npedal brek dan tekan.\nLANGKAH 2  \nLetakkan tuil anjakan ke kedudukan N.\nLANGKAH 3  \nSelepas memperlahankan kenderaan, hentikan \nkenderaan di tempat yang selamat di tepi jalan.\nLANGKAH 4  \nMatikan enjin (atau sistem hibrid).\nLANGKAH 5  \nAlihkan alas kaki.\n[Jika tuil anjakan tidak boleh dialihkan ke N
    ] \nLANGKAH 1  \nTeruskan menekan pedal brek dengan kedua-\ndua belah kaki untuk mengurangkan kelajuan'), Document(metadata={'id': 'safety manual.pdf_p24_c1', 'source': 'safety manual.pdf', 'page_number': 24, 'start_line_number': 2, 'end_line_number': 31
    }, page_content='LANGKAH 1  \nTeruskan menekan pedal brek dengan kedua-\ndua belah kaki untuk mengurangkan kelajuan \nsebanyak mana yang boleh.\nLANGKAH 2A  \nKenderaan dengan sistem kunci pintar: Matikan \nenjin (atau sistem hibrid) dengan menekan \ndan menahan suis “ENGINE START STOP \n(atau POWER)” selama 3 saat atau lebih.\nLANGKAH 2B  \nKenderaan tanpa sistem kunci pintar: \nMatikan enjin dengan memutar suis enjin \nke kedudukan “ACC”.\nLANGKAH 3  \nHentikan kenderaan di tempat yang \nselamat di tepi jalan.\nLANGKAH 4'), Document(metadata={'id': 'safety manual.pdf_p24_c2', 'source': 'safety manual.pdf', 'page_number': 24, 'start_line_number': 7, 'end_line_number': 40
    }, page_content='LANGKAH 3  \nHentikan kenderaan di tempat yang \nselamat di tepi jalan.\nLANGKAH 4  \nTanggalkan alas kaki.\nJIKA PEDAL PEMECUT TERSEKAT DI BAWAH ALAS KAKI \nDAN IA SUKAR DILEPASKAN \nMENUKAR ANJAKAN\n•  Letakkan tuil anjakan di kedudukan yang sesuai untuk keadaan \npemanduan yang berkenaan. Ketika di cerun, jangan biarkan \nkenderaan berguling ke belakang sementara tuil anjakan berada \ndi kedudukan memandu, atau berguling ke hadapan sementara \nanjakan berada di kedudukan R. Jika berbuat demikian anda'), Document(metadata={'id': 'safety manual.pdf_p24_c3', 'source': 'safety manual.pdf', 'page_number': 24, 'start_line_number': 40, 'end_line_number': 43
    }, page_content='anjakan berada di kedudukan R. Jika berbuat demikian anda \nboleh menyebabkan enjin terhenti, mengakibatkan prestasi brek \nberkurangan dengan teruk dan menjadikan stereng amat sukar \ndiputar dan ini boleh mengakibatkan kemalangan yang serius.'), Document(metadata={'id': 'safety manual.pdf_p25_c0', 'source': 'safety manual.pdf', 'page_number': 25, 'start_line_number': 1, 'end_line_number': 92
    }, page_content='25\nBAHAYA KEBAKARAN JIKA KENDERAAN DIBANJIRI  \nATAU TENGGELAM\n•  Jika air memasuki ruang enjin, enjin mungkin rosak dan \npenembusan air ke dalam sistem elektrik mungkin menyebabkan \nlitar pintas atau kebakaran.\n•  Jika kenderaan tenggelam di dalam hujan lebat, jangan hidupkan \nenjin untuk mengelakkan kerosakan selanjutnya. Tolak kenderaan \ndengan tangan jika anda perlu menggerakkan kenderaan anda. \nMintalah wakil penjual atau perkhidmatan tepi jalan untuk \nmembantu anda.'), Document(metadata={'id': 'safety manual.pdf_p25_c1', 'source': 'safety manual.pdf', 'page_number': 25, 'start_line_number': 10, 'end_line_number': 92
    }, page_content='Mintalah wakil penjual atau perkhidmatan tepi jalan untuk \nmembantu anda.\n•  Jangan pandu kenderaan secara paksa di jalan yang dibanjiri \nair walaupun melalui air cetek. Air boleh terpercik ke atas dan \nmemasuki ruang enjin.\nJIKA KENDERAAN TENGGELAM, KELUARLAH DARI \nKENDERAAN DENGAN TENANG\n•  Buka kancing tali pinggang keledar anda.\n•  Jika air tidak menghalang anda daripada membuka pintu, \nbukalah pintu dan keluar dari kenderaan dengan segera.'), Document(metadata={'id': 'safety manual.pdf_p25_c2', 'source': 'safety manual.pdf', 'page_number': 25, 'start_line_number': 19, 'end_line_number': 92
    }, page_content='bukalah pintu dan keluar dari kenderaan dengan segera.\n•  Jika anda tidak dapat membuka pintu, panjat keluar melalui \ntingkap. Jika tingkap tidak dapat dibuka, pecahkan cermin dan \npanjat keluar dengan berhati-hati. Jangan cuba memecahkan \ncermin depan untuk keluar dari kenderaan.\n•  Jika anda tidak dapat memecahkan tingkap, tunggulah sehingga \nkenderaan itu dibanjiri ke tahap yang tiada perbezaan tekanan \nair antara bahagian dalam dengan bahagian luar kenderaan,'), Document(metadata={'id': 'safety manual.pdf_p25_c3', 'source': 'safety manual.pdf', 'page_number': 25, 'start_line_number': 26, 'end_line_number': 102
    }, page_content='air antara bahagian dalam dengan bahagian luar kenderaan, \nkemudian dengan serta-merta keluar melalui pintu.\nBUKU PANDUAN KESELAMATAN INI BOLEH DIGUNAKAN \nUNTUK SEMUA KENDERAAN\n•  Terdapat amaran khusus untuk kenderaan hibrid seperti bahagian \nvoltan tinggi. Untuk mendapatkan amaran khusus bagi setiap \nkenderaan, rujuklah manual pemilik bagi kenderaan anda.\n 14  BERHATI-HATI SEMASA MEMANDU DAN BERHENTI\nBRAKE\nFORCE\nBRAKE\nFORCE\nWithout VSC\nWithout Brake Assist\nWithout ABS\nWith ABS\nBraking Point'), Document(metadata={'id': 'safety manual.pdf_p25_c4', 'source': 'safety manual.pdf', 'page_number': 25, 'start_line_number': 34, 'end_line_number': 102
    }, page_content='BRAKE\nFORCE\nBRAKE\nFORCE\nWithout VSC\nWithout Brake Assist\nWithout ABS\nWith ABS\nBraking Point\nWith Brake Assist\nWithout VSC\nWith VSC\nBA\nWithout TRC With TRC\nWithout VSC\nFront wheel slipping\nSteering loses control\nWithout VSC\nRear wheel slipping\nOver-steering\nWith VSC\nWith ABS\nWithout ABS\nBRAKE\nFORCE\nBRAKE\nFORCE\nWithout VSC\nWithout Brake Assist\nWithout ABS\nWith ABS\nBraking Point\nWith Brake Assist\nWithout VSC\nWith VSC\nBA\nWithout TRC With TRC\nWithout VSC\nFront wheel slipping\nSteering loses control'), Document(metadata={'id': 'safety manual.pdf_p25_c5', 'source': 'safety manual.pdf', 'page_number': 25, 'start_line_number': 34, 'end_line_number': 102
    }, page_content='With VSC\nBA\nWithout TRC With TRC\nWithout VSC\nFront wheel slipping\nSteering loses control\nWithout VSC\nRear wheel slipping\nOver-steering\nWith VSC\nWith ABS\nWithout ABS\nBRAKE\nFORCE\nBRAKE\nFORCE\nWithout VSC\nWithout Brake Assist\nWithout ABS\nWith ABS\nBraking Point\nWith Brake Assist\nWithout VSC\nWith VSC\nBA\nWithout TRC With TRC\nWithout VSC\nFront wheel slipping\nSteering loses control\nWithout VSC\nRear wheel slipping\nOver-steering\nWith VSC\nWith ABS\nWithout ABS')
]